{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>אמרות</b> — And the meaning: Because HaShem will save from the hand of those who exalt themselves with their tongue him who meditates on His Torah, therefore You will guard them." "And the word בעליל has a doubled lamed, like סגריר, and it is from the root ובעל הארץ, which is אדניה, and it will be כסף צרוף — the silver of the lord of the land." "<b>שבעתים</b> — Many times."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The text appears compressed or possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally. The letter-clause 'ובעל הארץ' and the form בעליל are obscure as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:11.089813930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}